<LevelHeader>
  type = Level
  name = The Siege Cleric
  description = 
  timestamp = 133687403248126564
</LevelHeader>
<Tips>
  The Siege Cleric is absurdly resistant to your usual ways of doing damage, and too big to defenestrate. There's a new possibility here.
  There's someone else here who is not friendly to the Chapel, he's just a little indisposed. One of you has the power to help with that.
  Once you've resurrected the Druid Hitman, use his Brittling Dart on the Siege Cleric to make it more vulnerable, both to direct damage and slam damage.
  Brittling Dart gets much more effective if you stack it up before dealing damage: try to hit the Cleric with 3 of them before dealing damage.
  Zan's regular shot, Banks' Spectral Skull, and Rion's Rabid Bite all deal direct damage that benefits from Brittle.
  Brittling Dart can be used many times in one turn, if you have the mana. Have Rion grab Intel, seal doors, and use Steal Mana to fund it.
  It might make sense to focus on sealing doors until you have your metaphorical ducks in a row to focus on the Cleric: he's a less immediate threat.
</Tips>

